<title>USA: Compaq Q3 inventories down $855 mln, cash up.</title>
<headline>Compaq Q3 inventories down $855 mln, cash up.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compaq Computer Corp said its inventories in the third quarter fell by $855 million to $1.4 billion, as part of its continuing focus on asset management.</p>
<p>Compaq, the world's largest personal computer maker, said its inventory turns -- the number of times it sold and replaced product -- increased to 9.0 in the third quarter from 5.1 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Compaq said these operational improvements lifted its cash balance to $3.2 billion, up 185 percent from a year ago.</p>
<p>The company today reported third quarter earnings of $1.25 a share, up from $0.89 a year ago.</p>
